      ("Can cast iron gutters be repaired or do they always need replacing?", "Cast iron on a Dublin period house is usually worth repairing in matching sections rather than replacing the lot. Pitted rust on the surface is repairable by welding and repainting. Rust through the base of the section is not, and that section has to be swapped."),
